# groups.txt -- step 13, anchors-joinsplit-parameters (upstream v1.0.0-beta.3).
#
# name <tab> kind <tab> weight <tab> crate <tab> arg
#
#   kind   gate    proof of life + inherited regression. Binary, earns nothing,
#                  vetoes the whole step. Weight column MUST be 0.
#          scored  this step's new capability + peripheral breadth. Positive
#                  integer weight; the scored weights sum to 100.
#   crate  a crate name -> driver group; arg is the exact number of test cases
#          @build       -> build group;  arg is a whole cargo invocation
#
#   reward = gate x score
#
# Gate groups carry no weight on purpose. Pricing inherited work is what let a
# no-op collect a share of the score; under this model it collects nothing.
#
# The arg column for driver groups is the number of `#[test]` functions the
# driver defines; every count below was read back off the validated driver
# with `grep -c '^#\[test\]'` after the driver passed against the oracle tree.
#
# workspace-checks uses --all-features because zebra-chain/benches/block.rs
# reaches zebra_chain::block::tests::generate, which block.rs gates behind
# #[cfg(any(test, feature = "bench"))]; a bench target is not built with
# cfg(test), so the plain --all-targets form does not compile at this tag.

